{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RegTraceGramNondegenerate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RegTraceGramNondegenerate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RegTraceGram","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TracePi","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.SimpleRing.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.SimpleRing.Matrix"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceGram_det_ne_zero_of_algEquiv_pi_matrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceGram_det_ne_zero_of_algEquiv_pi_matrix","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGramNondegenerate.lean#L243-L253","doc":"**Gram determinant nonzero, in any basis.**  The determinant form of the statement above:\nthis is what a `T_w`-basis Gram computation was needed for, now supplied by semisimplicity\nrather than by the Schur-element product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceBilin_nondegenerate_of_algEquiv_pi_matrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceBilin_nondegenerate_of_algEquiv_pi_matrix","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGramNondegenerate.lean#L226-L241","doc":"**The assembled statement.**\n\nAn algebra carrying an isomorphism onto a finite product of matrix algebras over a\ncharacteristic-zero field has nondegenerate regular trace form.  Combined with\n`LinearMap.BilinForm.nondegenerate_iff_det_ne_zero` this says its Gram determinant is nonzero in\n*every* basis — which is the non-vanishing half of Geck–Pfeiffer 7.2.6, obtained without\ncomputing the Schur-element product.\n\nThis is the exact shape `QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeWedderburn` supplies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceBilin_nondegenerate_matrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceBilin_nondegenerate_matrix","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGramNondegenerate.lean#L212-L224","doc":"**The regular trace form of a matrix algebra over a characteristic-zero field is\nnondegenerate.**\n\n`Matrix ι ι K` is simple for nonempty `ι` (`IsSimpleRing.matrix` over the simple ring `K`), so\n`regTraceBilin_nondegenerate_of_isSimpleRing_charZero` applies.  Empty `ι` is the zero ring and\nis handled separately — it is *not* simple (simplicity requires `Nontrivial`), but its form is\nnondegenerate for the trivial reason that `0` is its only element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceBilin_nondegenerate_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceBilin_nondegenerate_pi","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGramNondegenerate.lean#L190-L210","doc":"**Nondegeneracy is inherited from the blocks of a finite product.**\n\nTesting an `x` against `y = Pi.single j w` kills every summand of `regTraceForm_pi` but the\n`j`-th, so the hypothesis at index `j` forces `x j = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceForm_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceForm_pi","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGramNondegenerate.lean#L176-L188","doc":"**The regular trace form of a finite product is the sum of the blocks' forms.**\n\n`L_x` on `∀ i, B i` is block-diagonal with blocks `L_{x i}`, so `QOU.MathlibExt.trace_piDiag`\napplies.  Mathlib covers only the binary case (`LinearMap.trace_prodMap'`); the `∀ i` version\nis in `QOU.MathlibExt.TracePi`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceBilin_nondegenerate_of_isSimpleRing_charZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceBilin_nondegenerate_of_isSimpleRing_charZero","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGramNondegenerate.lean#L158-L168","doc":"**Simple + characteristic zero ⟹ the regular trace form is nondegenerate.**\n\nThe dimension hypothesis of `regTraceBilin_nondegenerate_of_isSimpleRing` is automatic here:\n`B(1,1) = finrank K A` by `regTraceForm_one_one`, and a nontrivial finite-dimensional algebra\nhas positive dimension, which is nonzero in `K` exactly because `K` has characteristic zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceBilin_nondegenerate_of_isSimpleRing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceBilin_nondegenerate_of_isSimpleRing","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGramNondegenerate.lean#L140-L156","doc":"**Nondegeneracy of the regular trace form on a simple ring, given `B(1,1) ≠ 0`.**\n\nThe radical is a two-sided ideal (`regTraceRadical`), so simplicity forces it to be `⊥` or\n`⊤`; `⊤` would put `1` in it and give `B(1, 1) = 0`.  This is the converse of\n`isSemisimpleRing_of_regTraceBilin_nondegenerate`, and it is the direction that makes the\nGram-determinant *computation* unnecessary for non-vanishing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.mem_regTraceRadical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.mem_regTraceRadical","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGramNondegenerate.lean#L136-L138","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceRadical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceRadical","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGramNondegenerate.lean#L112-L134","doc":"**The radical of the regular trace form, as a two-sided ideal.**\n\n`{x | ∀ y, B(x, y) = 0}`.  Closure on the right is `regTraceForm_mul_assoc`; closure on the\nleft needs it *together with* the symmetry `regTraceForm_comm`, since the form is only\nassociative in the shape `B(xy, z) = B(x, yz)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceForm_one_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceForm_one_one","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGramNondegenerate.lean#L100-L110","doc":"**`B(1, 1)` is the dimension.**  `L_1 = id`, so the trace is `finrank K A` in `K`.\n\nThis is the whole of the characteristic input: the radical argument below excludes the\ndegenerate case by `B(1,1) ≠ 0`, and `B(1,1)` is a *natural number cast into `K`*.  In\ncharacteristic `p ∣ finrank K A` it vanishes and the argument genuinely fails — as it must,\nsince the Gram determinant of a semisimple algebra really does vanish there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceForm_mul_assoc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceForm_mul_assoc","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGramNondegenerate.lean#L93-L98","doc":"**Associativity of the regular trace form.**  Both sides are `trace (L_z)` for the same\n`z`, by `mul_assoc`.  This is what makes the form's radical a *two-sided* ideal rather than\nmerely a subspace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceBilin_nondegenerate_congr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceBilin_nondegenerate_congr","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGramNondegenerate.lean#L76-L91","doc":"**Nondegeneracy of the regular trace form transports along an algebra isomorphism.**\n\nThis is the step that lets a Gram determinant on one presentation of an algebra be settled\non another — here, transporting from the Wedderburn block product back to the `T_w` basis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceForm_algEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceForm_algEquiv","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGramNondegenerate.lean#L62-L74","doc":"**The regular trace form is an algebra invariant.**\n\n`L_{e x} = e ∘ L_x ∘ e⁻¹` as a `K`-linear endomorphism, so the two traces agree by\n`LinearMap.trace_conj'`.  Stated for the *product* `x * y` directly, since that is the shape\n`regTraceForm` is defined in. ","signatureChunk":0}]}